  "When you request deletion of your data, we remove the identifying fields from our systems rather than deleting the record outright. This means that your name, email address, account identifier, IP address, and user agent are permanently removed, while your query history, consent record, and aggregated usage data remain without any of those fields attached to them. This is deliberate, and it leaves us a record of Platform usage while removing what identifies you.",
  "Where you withdraw your consent, or request erasure, any Document you have uploaded and any output generated in response to your queries shall cease to be accessible at the time your request takes effect, subject to the retention periods applicable to Anthropic PBC as described in this Privacy Policy.",
  "Under the DPDP Rules, personal data must be erased when the purpose for which it was collected is fulfilled or when you withdraw your consent, and Data Fiduciaries are required to retain processing logs for at least one year even after erasure. Backups qualify any deletion promise, and our nightly database dumps are retained for approximately one week, and infrastructure snapshots for four weeks, so a person erased today persists in backups for up to four weeks.",
  "We shall inform you at least forty-eight (48) hours before erasing your Personal Data because the purpose for which it was collected has been fulfilled, giving you a final opportunity to exercise your rights under the DPDP Act. This notice is required under Rule 8 of the DPDP Rules, 2025, and we shall send it to the email address associated with your account. If you do not respond to the notice within forty-eight (48) hours, we shall proceed with the erasure of your Personal Data in accordance with this Privacy Policy and the Data Retention Policy.",
  "Your personal data is stored on servers located in India. However, when you sign in through the authentication provider, the identity verification exchange may occur on the authentication provider's infrastructure, which may involve a cross-border transfer. Where you sign in with a one-time password over WhatsApp, your phone number is processed by Meta Platforms, Inc. and its affiliates on infrastructure outside India for the sole purpose of delivering that message. When you submit a query, the extracted text from your Document is transmitted to Anthropic PBC, the provider of the Claude API, which processes the data on infrastructure located outside India.",
  "We ensure that any cross-border transfer of personal data is subject to appropriate safeguards as required under applicable Data Protection Laws, including by entering into contractual arrangements with the recipients of the data that require them to provide a level of protection to the data that is no less than the level of protection required under the DPDP Act, and by entering into the Data Processing Addendum with Anthropic PBC.",
