  "DataDost has appointed a Data Protection Officer who is responsible for overseeing the protection of your personal data and for addressing any questions, concerns, or complaints you may have in relation to your personal data, the exercise of any of your rights under the DPDP Act, or the conduct of any Data Processor engaged by DataDost.",
  "You may contact the Data Protection Officer at: Data Protection Officer, Santosh Dave, Email: privacy@datadost.in. The Data Protection Officer will acknowledge your complaint within two (2) business days and will use best efforts to resolve it within fifteen (15) business days from the date of receipt. If you are not satisfied with the response of the Data Protection Officer, you have the right to escalate your complaint to the Data Protection Board of India, as provided under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.",
  "DataDost has also appointed a Grievance Officer who is responsible for addressing any questions, concerns, or complaints the User may have regarding the Platform, the services provided by DataDost, the Subscription, the Subscription Fee, or the refund of any Subscription Fee. You may contact the Grievance Officer at: Grievance Officer, Email: grievance@datadost.in. The Grievance Officer will acknowledge your complaint within two (2) business days and will use best efforts to resolve it within fifteen (15) business days from the date of receipt. If you are not satisfied with the response of the Grievance Officer, you have the right to escalate the complaint to the Data Protection Board of India, in respect of any matter relating to the processing of your Personal Data, or to the appropriate consumer forum, in respect of any matter relating to the Subscription or to the refund of any Subscription Fee.",
  "Where you are uncertain as to whether a complaint should be addressed to the Data Protection Officer or to the Grievance Officer, you may address the complaint to either officer, and that officer shall forward the complaint to the other officer if the matter falls within the other officer's remit, and shall inform you of the forwarding. The timelines applicable to the resolution of the complaint shall run from the date on which the complaint is received by the officer to whom it is ultimately addressed.",
